sequenceDiagram
    participant LLM as LLM Agent
    participant MCP as MCP Tool
    participant TH as Thymus
    participant EV as Evidence (read-only)
    participant LOG as Audit Log

    rect rgb(219, 234, 254)
    Note over LLM,LOG: A. LEGIT READ — in-bounds evidence path
    LLM->>MCP: read /cases/img.E01
    MCP->>TH: check_read /cases/img.E01
    TH-->>MCP: ALLOW (allowlist match)
    MCP->>EV: open bytes (read-only)
    EV-->>MCP: image bytes
    MCP-->>LLM: bytes returned
    MCP->>LOG: log ALLOW read
    end

    rect rgb(254, 226, 226)
    Note over LLM,LOG: B. MODEL TRIES TO WRITE OR MUTATE EVIDENCE
    LLM->>MCP: write or mutate /cases/img.E01
    MCP->>TH: check_write (the only write path)
    TH-->>MCP: REJECT, all writes forbidden (hard-coded)
    Note over EV: Nothing reaches Evidence, no byte mutated
    MCP-->>LLM: denied, no write tool exists
    MCP->>LOG: log REJECT_WRITE
    end

    rect rgb(254, 226, 226)
    Note over LLM,LOG: C. MODEL TRIES OUT-OF-BOUNDS READ (/etc/shadow or ..)
    LLM->>MCP: read /etc/shadow or ../secret
    MCP->>TH: check_read (allowlist plus traversal guards)
    TH-->>MCP: REJECT before any I/O (not on allowlist)
    Note over EV: No open, no bytes read
    MCP-->>LLM: denied
    MCP->>LOG: log REJECT
    end

    Note over LLM,LOG: The capability does not exist — there is no write tool for the model to misuse. Integrity is architectural, not a prompt the model could ignore.
